cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ADEPT, please cite it as below."
title: "ADEPT: Automated Diagnostic-adequacy Evaluation and Prioritization of Tissue"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-01
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sjarso1/adept-microscopy"
abstract: >-
  Closed-loop autonomous microscopy on the OpenFlexure platform for breast
  core-needle biopsy telepathology in low- and middle-income countries.
  ADEPT assesses specimen adequacy against five formal criteria in a
  canonical, instrument-independent image space, drives targeted
  high-resolution re-acquisition, ranks regions of interest, and packages
  the result for remote pathologist review. All models are validated
  leave-one-instrument-out.
keywords:
  - digital pathology
  - telepathology
  - OpenFlexure
  - breast biopsy
  - specimen adequacy
  - stain normalization
  - multiple-instance learning
  - global health
